l":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/milestones/7","html_url":"https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/milestone/7","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/milestones/7/labels","id":453043,"node_id":"MDk6TWlsZXN0b25lNDUzMDQz","number":7,"title":"3.0.0","description":"New major release that breaks compatibility with 2.x\r\n\r\n- PHP5.4.19+\r\n- New ORM & behaviors.\r\n- Improved Routing\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":30,"created_at":"2014-11-07T23:04:18Z","updated_at":"2014-12-03T14:45:16Z","closed_at":"2014-11-23T03:53:08Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have an issue really hard to simulate, but:\nThe application is being used by more than 300 users at the same time. They are using it all day so there are alot of queries. And sometimes happens, that in one-to-many relations the record is not assigned correctly to it's _parent_ but the the different _parent_ or the parent_id is NULL.\n\nFor example having **Articles** and **Comments** when adding new comment I do something like this:\n\n``` PHP\n$newComment = $this -> Articles -> Comments -> newEntity( $data );\n$article = $this -> Articles -> get( $id, [ 'contain' => [ 'Comments' ] ]);\n$article -> comments = array_merge( (array)$article -> comments, (array)$newComment );\n$this -> Articles -> save( $article );\n```\n\nThe _issue_ is that $newComment is bind to different article or the _article_id_ is NULL.\n\nI'm not sure if it is the correct way to add one item. I've read, that if I do\n\n``` PHP\n$this -> comments = [ $newComment ];\n```\n\nit will overwrite other comments, so therefore I am mergin. I know, I can save only that new comment:\n\n``` PHP\n$newComment -> article_id = $id;\n$this -> Articles -> Comments -> save( $newComment );\n```\n\nBut this doesn't really solve the issue and my usage is more complex, so I need to bind the **new comment** to the **article**, do some stuff and then save it together.\n\nI am using **MSSQL**. What I ask you is maybe to investigate if there could be any problem with getting IDs. For example if there is an _INSERT/UPDATE_ request followed by other _GET_LAST_ID_ request, is it possible that other _INSERT/UPDATE_ request could be inbetween and mess things up? Because that's what happen to me.\n\nThis _doesnt happen always_, only during the day when _everybody is using_ the application. So therefore I suppose it must be a problem with multiple parallel requests.\n\nCould you please show me, which _methods/files_ are responsible for _saving_? And how the process of saving _associations_ goes. Maybe there's something wrong, but I couldnt find it by myself.\n\nThanks for any help!\n","closed_by":{"login":"markstory","id":24086,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory","html_url":"https://github.com/markstory","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/markstory/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/use